                        <field name="dc_description">Composite manuscript from the Dominican Cloister Maria Himmelskron in Hochheim near Worms, containing works by Johannes Meyer; according to a note of ownership in his own hand, it was written in 1474. The Dominican Johannes Meyer of Basel acted as confessor in women’s convents of Strict Observance and put his extensive historiographic work in the service of the 14th century reform of the Dominican Order. </field>
